body:
I created a very simple custom module (just for testing) called bakend.
Then added a link to it in the layout menu but cannot get the menu item being activated when I visit the module.
I see the route in the module is being created with a preceding slash, when the site controller one is not.
Is this the expected behavior?

Config:

``` php
...
'modules' => array(
    'debug' => array(
        'class' => 'yii\debug\Module',
        'enabled' => YII_DEBUG && YII_ENV === 'dev',
    ),
    'backend' => array(
        'class' => 'app\modules\backend\Module',
    ),
),
...
```

Main layout (using it in the module):

``` php
echo Menu::widget(array(
    'options' => array('class' => 'nav'),
    'items' => array(
        array('label' => 'Home', 'url' => array('/site/index')),
        array('label' => 'Backend', 'url' => array('/backend/default/index'), 'visible' => !Yii::$app->user->isGuest),
        Yii::$app->user->isGuest ?
            array('label' => 'Login', 'url' => array('/site/login')) :
            array('label' => 'Logout (' . Yii::$app->user->identity->username .')' , 'url' => array('/site/logout')),
    ),
)); 
```

Check in the `yii\widgets\Menu` returning false:

``` php
protected function isItemActive($item)
{
    // The third check here is returning false
    if (isset($item['url']) && is_array($item['url']) && trim($item['url'][0], '/') === $this->route) {
        unset($item['url']['#']);
        if (count($item['url']) > 1) {
            foreach (array_splice($item['url'], 1) as $name => $value) {
                if (!isset($this->params[$name]) || $this->params[$name] != $value) {
                    return false;
                }
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}
```

